abstract: >
  Yin-Yang Convergence Window Protocol v0.1.0 is a draft structural protocol
  for convergence window design, phase stability scoring, amplitude threshold
  control, rebalance timing, overcorrection prevention, settling period control,
  and stability decisions in oscillating reasoning systems. It extends the
  reasoning-control lineage of Yin-Yang Five-Phase Reasoning Protocol and
  Yin-Yang Oscillation Control Protocol by focusing on when oscillating
  reasoning has become stable enough to stop, delay, return, rebalance, or
  continue minimally.

